.SH NAME
abacus-mcp-server - Start MCP server for Claude Code integration


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBabacus mcp-server [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server on stdio, exposing abacus tools for scanning, querying, matching, and managing the application graph.

.PP
Designed to be launched by Claude Code or other MCP-compatible clients. The
server communicates over stdin/stdout using the MCP JSON-RPC protocol.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Path to abacus config file (default: .abacus/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mcp-server


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--db\fP=".abacus/abacus.db"
	Path to the database file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output in JSON format

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Enable verbose output


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  $ abacus mcp-server
  $ abacus mcp-server --config .abacus/config.yaml
  $ abacus mcp-server --db ./custom/path/abacus.db
.EE


